      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To evaluate the association between the methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase C/T polymorphism and the prevalence and course of asthma."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHOD",
          "content": "Genotypes were determined in 433 asthmatic patients and 1 249 healthy subjects by the polymerase chain reaction and restriction fragment length polymorphism method."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The frequencies of the three genotypes were 40.27% for CC, 48.44% for CT, 11.29% for TT and the frequency of allelic T was 35.51% in controls. The frequency of TT genotype in atopic asthmatic patients was significantly higher than that in controls (P = 0.026). The OR for the TT genotype compared with all CC and CT genotypes was 1.61 (95% CI 1.06 approximately 2.47)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "These results imply that homozygosity for this common mutation significantly increases the risk of atopic asthma."
        }
      ]},
